{
  "A checkbox with its caption: checked, unchecked or indeterminate, three states on request, read-only, required and checked with its group. A native checkbox underneath, drawn from the design tokens.": "",
  "Checked, unchecked, indeterminate": "",
  "`null` shows the indeterminate dash. A click on it checks the box; with `threeState` the user goes through all three: unchecked → checked → indeterminate.": "",
  "A box over a list is indeterminate while only some items are checked. Its value is a function of the list; a click on it checks or unchecks them all.": "",
  "The caption sits after the box, or before it with `labelPosition=\"start\"`. With `stretch` the field takes the width, so a box after its caption goes to the far end, as in a settings list. `labelMode=\"hidden\"` keeps the caption for screen readers only.": "",
  "Required": "",
  "`required` means the box must be checked. It is checked with its group, like any field: the first box left unchecked gets focus.": "",
  "Toggles it (the native checkbox key).": "",
  "Focuses and toggles it (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "One stop per checkbox.": "",
  "A native `<input type=\"checkbox\">` drawn with `appearance: none`; its caption is a `<label for>`, so a click on the caption toggles it.": "",
  "The native `indeterminate` state: read out as \"mixed\".": "",
  "`aria-invalid=\"true\"`; the line under the caption is a polite live region and describes the box.": "",
  "The design system focus ring, for the keyboard only.": "",
  "The checkbox writes no text of its own; the `required` message comes from `uiLocale.strings`, and a message already shown follows a change at once.": "",
  "The field. `data-state` (`checked`, `unchecked`, `mixed`), `data-label-position`, `data-size`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`.": "",
  "The layout CheckBox and Switch share: the box and its caption side by side.": "",
  "The native checkbox: the box itself.": "",
  "The mark drawn over the box.": "",
  "The caption and the line under it.": "",
  "Unit: the box, with every state (`checked`, `mixed`, `invalid`, each with `-hover`, `-pressed`, `-focus`; `disabled`, `checked-disabled`).": "",
  "Units: the check mark, the dash of a mixed box, and a layer over the box (`pressed`, `disabled`).": "",
  "Units: a halo centred on the box (`checked`, `hover`, `focus`, `pressed`) and a ring round the box and its caption under the keys, where the language has them.": "",
  "Units: the caption (`disabled`) and the row it sits in.": "",
  "The box and its mark, per size.": "",
  "The space before the caption, how far a press moves the box, and what the ring under the keys goes round (`box` or `item`).": "",
  "`true` checked, `false` unchecked, `null` indeterminate. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "The caption next to the box; `&Name` makes Alt+N toggle it. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "The caption after the box (`end`) or before it (`start`), in the reading direction.": "",
  "`hidden` keeps the caption for screen readers only; every other mode shows it next to the box.": "",
  "A click goes unchecked → checked → indeterminate. Without it a click only checks and unchecks; code can still set `null`.": "",
  "Focusable and read out, but a click or Space changes nothing.": "",
  "It must be checked: a mark after the caption, `aria-required` and a `required` rule.": "",
  "Fills the width of what it sits in; with `labelPosition=\"start\"` the box goes to the far end.": "",
  "The native `<input type=\"checkbox\">`.": "",
  "Changes the value as a click does (with `threeState`, to the next of the three).": "",
  "Focuses the box.": "",
  "The value changed. `e`: `{ value, previousValue, byUser, source, event? }`; `null` stays `null`.": "",
  "`ToggleField`, the base CheckBox and Switch share (the caption next to a native checkbox, read-only, the access key), is exported for controls of your own.": ""
}
